  "query_preview": "/SATURDAY THROUGH WEDNESDAY/...\nIssued at 330 AM CDT Thu Aug 20 2026\n\nUpper ridging across the Rockies begins to slowly amplify into the \nweekend, with the ridge axis beginning to move into the Plains by \nSunday night. This will lead to warmer temperatures both Sunday\nand Monday, with highs in the lower 90s across western and \nsouthwest Nebraska. The approach of this ridge axis will also \nfinally lead to weaker flow aloft, and lesser wind shear for at \nleast a couple of days across the area. This suggests a brief \nreprieve from the recent daily threat for strong to severe \nstorms. That said, sub-severe thunderstorms cannot be ruled out \neach day as we head into the weekend. \n\nAs we head into next week, the upper ridge begins to flatten out \nacross the southwestern US and brings a return of increasing \nnorthwesterly flow aloft across the Plains. This could bring a \nreturn of a threat for strong to severe storms, as wind shear \nincreases again in response to the strengthening northwest flow. \nMesoscale details will need to be resolved with respect to this \nthreat, though it appears the active pattern will continue across \nthe area as we head into next week.",
